# IA Engineering local state — not part of the framework
.omc/

# Generated runtime agent definitions (Adapters/ai-runtimes/generate-agents.sh).
# Derived from Employees/ and Registry/employees.yml, so they are build
# artifacts rather than sources: 42 files of ~210 lines each is roughly 9,000
# lines of derived content in a repository whose entire source is ~15,000, and
# every Employee edit would produce a large mechanical diff beside the real one.
#
# The cost is real — a fresh clone must run the generator before the Employees
# exist as dispatchable agents, the same way it must run install.sh before the
# hooks exist. A project that prefers them present on clone should commit them
# and add `generate-agents.sh --check` to CI. See Adapters/ai-runtimes/README.md.
.claude/agents/

# Standards/DATA_PROTECTION_STANDARD.md — real data lives only in the local
# data directory, secrets only in the environment, operational state is never
# committed. Adapters/git-hooks/pre-commit and data-policy.yml refuse the same
# paths; this is the layer that keeps `git add -A` from staging them at all.
local_test_data/
.env
# The whole directory, not only the state file. `.ia-engineering/` is where a
# project keeps what is true of it right now — its dated state, its release
# drafts, its per-pole working notes — and all of it is the same category:
# operational, local, and not part of the framework it sits beside. The
# Adapter installs the SESSION_STATE.md line into an adopting project; this
# repository ignores the directory because it is also its own first adopter.
.ia-engineering/
